249:             "bodyMarkdown": "A useful planner separates **data**, **selection**, **formatting**, and **output** instead of mixing every responsibility together.

This library example uses the same ideas without giving away the event project:

```js
const books = [
  { title: "North Star", available: true },
  { title: "Deep Blue", available: false }
];

function isAvailable(book) {
  return book.available;
}

function labelBook(book) {
  return `Book: ${book.title}`;
}

const availableBooks = books.filter(isAvailable);
const labels = availableBooks.map(labelBook);

for (const label of labels) {
  console.log(label);
}
```

Step by step:

1. The array stores structured object records.
2. `isAvailable` returns a boolean, so `filter` can use it as a selection callback.
3. `labelBook` returns text, so `map` can transform each selected object.
4. `for...of` visits the finished labels and displays them.

The project uses this same **shape of thinking**, but with campus events and different function names."

